From: Robert Jefe Lindstaedt <robert.lindstaedt@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 16:49:02 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Fit bounds on the globe from any start, centred and filling
 the padding

fitBounds and cameraForBounds on the globe projection missed in three ways
(#5439):

- the camera helper was chosen by the projection at the current zoom, so a
  fit started past the globe-to-mercator transition was solved, and its
  jump or flight constrained, as mercator, landing far off for a target on
  the globe;
- the zoom was corrected by one scale step from the mercator answer and the
  center kept at the mercator middle, so country-scale bounds ended
  off-centre by up to 90 px and short of, or past, the padded viewport,
  sampled at corners and edge midpoints only;
- bounds given to the constructor were fitted before the style's projection
  was known.

The fit is now solved in the projection of the fitted zoom, and on the
sphere by a damped Newton iteration on the edges' screen offset and the
scale still needed, starting from the bounds' spherical middle and keeping
the first estimate when it is not improved. Jumps, eases and flights to a
zoom with the other projection are constrained by that projection. The
constructor fits again on the first style load unless the camera moved.
